            <div xml:id="d221-a6">

                <pb facs="0280" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg220"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">addition</hi>.</head>
                <p>As the clause concerning the anchorage of the schooner <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henry Crosby</hi> is deemed not sufficiently clear, it is acknowledged that
                    through bad information and unacquaintance, the vessel was anchored in a part of
                    the coast not recognized as a port of entry and uninhabitable.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. F. Stubbs</hi>.</p>
                <p>I certify to the above signature.</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hardy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States Consular Agent.</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consular
                        Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Azua, December 26, 1895</hi>.</p>
                <p>I, John Hardy, consular agent of the United States of America at Azua, certify
                    that this is a true copy of the original on the record books of this agency.</p>
                <p>Given under my hand and seal the day, month, and year above written.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hardy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consular Agent</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
